Regina REXX in lxa
==================

This directory holds the interpreter of Regina REXX 3.9.6
(https://regina-rexx.sourceforge.io/), used by lxa as the ARexx interpreter
(roadmap Phase 250). Regina is licensed under the GNU Library General Public
License (COPYING-LIB). It is NOT covered by lxa's MIT licence.

Only the files needed to build the interpreter are included. The build
(sys/CMakeLists.txt, REGINA_SOURCES) links them with lxa's ARexx glue
sys/System/ARexx.c into SYS:System/ARexx. RexxMast (sys/System/RexxMast.c)
starts one ARexx process per program.

lxa's changes
-------------

Every change to a Regina source is marked "LXA" and is mostly guarded by
LXA_AMIGA (defined in config.h):

  config.h, configur.h  configuration for m68k-amigaos-gcc/libnix
  error.c          ARexx error numbers and "+++ Error N in line L: text"
  builtin.c        the ARexx error texts (ERRORTEXT)
  funcs.c          only the built-in functions of ARexx 1.15
  arxfuncs.c       TRIM() fix; SHOW() through the glue
  client.c         RC of host commands; the function exit runs before
                   external routines (the ARexx Library List)
  envir.c          every host command goes to the RXCMD exit; RC, FAILAT
                   and command tracing as in ARexx
  interprt.c       lxa_arexx_poll() once per clause (HI, Ctrl-C, TS/TE);
                   ARexx option defaults
  files.c          the ARexx program search (current directory, REXX:)
  os_other.c       AmigaOS paths
  signals.c        no POSIX signals
  misc.c           C-locale character classes without locale.library
  lexsrc.c, extern.h  the large scanner buffers are allocated at start
                   (lxa_lex_buffers()), so the data/BSS image RexxMast
                   restores per program stays small

Files that are lxa's own code (MIT licence):

  lxa_hooks.c      the ARexx personality called from the patches above
  lxa_arexx.h      interface between Regina, lxa_hooks.c and ARexx.c
